  "body": "What happens:\nRotary Contour, Rotary Parallel, and Rotary Offset ignore face selection. They always generate toolpath over the full model. A user cannot contain the operation to selected faces.\n\nExpected:\nRotary operations accept selected faces as the geometry source. Toolpath generates only over the picked faces. The fitted axis still comes from the full model because the rotation axis must be the part's true rotation axis.\n\nEvidence:\nFound while testing Rotary Parallel with a face selection. The operation machines the whole model, not only the picked faces. The code excludes rotary ops from selection-driven regions in crates/app/src/operation/material_region.rs lines 251-257.\n\nDone means:\n- New operation kind \"Rotary Contour\", \"Rotary Parallel\", and \"Rotary Offset\" accept SrcRef::Selection as geometry source\n- Toolpath stays within the selected face boundaries\n- Axis fitting still uses the full model (the part's true rotation axis)\n- Stock simulation verifies only the generated toolpath\n- UI operation panel enables face selection for rotary ops\n- Non-cylindrical or disconnected selections refuse with a clear message\n- Full-model operation (no selection) still works identically\n- Tests cover selection-driven rotary generation and refusals",
